\ wsub.fam — sub-name certificates (docs/SUBNAME_CERT.md; docs/GUI_WALLET.md,
\ phase 3), as tabminer's subnames.rs: a name's owner signs, for a label,
\ a certificate naming the holder's id; in init mode a resolver asks the
\ owner (a query, KIND_SUBNAME_QUERY), which answers with the bundle it
\ holds (KIND_SUBNAME_ANSWER), checked against the chain.  Here only the
\ owner's own certificates count (case 1: the issuer key hashes to the
\ name's value); a bundle with a delegation (an issuer the owner named)
\ is refused for now.  After wkeys.fam and crypto/dilithium.fam.
\
\ A certificate: the name and the label (each its length, then its
\ bytes), the type (0 none, 1 an id), the value's length (u16) and the
\ value, seq (u64), expiry (u64), the issuer's Dilithium key, the
\ signature (context "tab-subname") over all before it.  A bundle: the
\ certificate's length (u32), the certificate, [a delegation].  A query:
\ the name and the label; an answer: the same, then a bundle or nothing.
\
\ sbinit  the buffers (once).
\ sbqry ( name nl label ll dst -- n )  a query's bytes.
\ sbcert ( dst -- n )  a certificate signed: sbnm/sbnl, sblb/sbll, sbkd
\ (the type), sbval (32 bytes, an id's), sbseq and sbexp (8 bytes each),
\ the issuer's key mgpk/mgsk.
\ sbans ( cert cn dst -- n )  an answer to the query read (sbnm.. set):
\ the name and label, then the bundle of the certificate (cn bytes; 0:
\ none).
\ sbpq ( a n -- ok )  a query: its name and label at sbnm/sbnl, sblb/sbll.
\ sbpa ( a n -- code )  an answer for the query sbnm/sblb: 0 malformed or
\ for another name, 1 no certificate, 2 a certificate at sbca (sbcn
\ bytes) with no delegation, 3 one with a delegation (not taken here).
\ sbvf ( cert cn value now -- ok )  a sound certificate for sbnm/sblb
\ from the owner whose id (32 canonical bytes) is value: the issuer the
\ key's hash, in force (and at most 30 days off), a well-formed value,
\ the signature holding; its type at sbtk, its value at sbtv.
\ sbbun ( a n -- ok )  a bundle as onion mode publishes and fetches it
\ (GET_CERT's answer; a certificate sent to its holder): its name and
\ label at sbnm/sbnl, sblb/sbll, its certificate at sbca (sbcn bytes); one
\ with a delegation after is refused, as sbpa's code 3.
\ sbpt ( dst -- )  the point id of the full name sblb.sbnm, whose
\ rendezvous points hold its certificate in onion mode (subnames.rs's
\ Cert::point: hash_domain(25, "label.name" packed)), 32 bytes.

: sbnm variable ;  : sbnl variable ;  : sblb variable ;  : sbll variable ;  : sbkd variable ;  : sbval variable ;
: sbseq variable ;  : sbexp variable ;  : sbca variable ;  : sbcn variable ;  : sbtk variable ;  : sbtv variable ;
: sbtn variable ;  : sbtl variable ;  : sbvn variable ;  : sbvv variable ;  : sbpk variable ;  : sbsg variable ;
: sbo variable ;  : sbp variable ;  : sbh variable ;  : sbw variable ;  : sbe variable ;  : sbt variable ;
: sbinit  sbnm @ 0= if 40 lit alloc sbtn !  40 lit alloc sbtl !  40 lit alloc sbnm !  40 lit alloc sblb !  20 lit alloc sbval !  8 lit alloc sbseq !  8 lit alloc sbexp !  20 lit alloc sbh !  20 lit alloc sbw ! then ;
: sbcp  ?dup if 0 lit do over i + c@ over i + c! loop then 2drop ;      \ ( src dst n -- )
: sbput  sbo @ c!  sbo @ 1 lit + sbo ! ;                               \ ( b -- )
: sbbytes  tuck sbo @ swap sbcp  sbo @ + sbo ! ;                       \ ( a n -- )
: sbputn  dup sbput sbbytes ;                                          \ ( a n -- )  its length, then it
: sbput32  4 lit 0 lit do dup i 3 lit lshift rshift sbput loop drop ;  \ ( x -- )
: sbput16  dup sbput 8 lit rshift sbput ;
: sble@  dup c@ over 1 lit + c@ 8 lit lshift or over 2 lit + c@ 10 lit lshift or swap 3 lit + c@ 18 lit lshift or ;
: sbsame  -1 lit swap 0 lit do 2 lit pick i + c@ 2 lit pick i + c@ = and loop nip nip ;   \ ( a b n -- flag )

: sbqry
sbo !  sbo @ sbp !  sbvn !  sbvv !  sbputn  sbvv @ sbvn @ sbputn  sbo @ sbp @ - ;
: sbcert
sbo !  sbo @ sbp !
sbnm @ sbnl @ sbputn  sblb @ sbll @ sbputn  sbkd @ sbput
sbkd @ 1 lit = if 20 lit sbput16  sbval @ 20 lit sbbytes else 0 lit sbput16 then
sbseq @ 8 lit sbbytes  sbexp @ 8 lit sbbytes  mgpk @ 7A0 lit sbbytes
mgsk @ sbp @ sbo @ sbp @ - "tab-subname" B lit sbo @ dilsign
sbo @ CED lit + sbp @ - ;
: sbans
sbo !  sbo @ sbp !  sbnm @ sbnl @ sbputn  sblb @ sbll @ sbputn
?dup if dup sbput32 sbbytes else drop then
sbo @ sbp @ - ;

\ Reading: sbp the place, sbe the end.
\ sbget ( dst -- len ok )  a name or label (1 to 32 bytes) to dst,
\ NUL-ended.
: sbget
sbt !
sbp @ sbe @ u< if
	sbp @ c@  dup 1 lit - 20 lit u<  over sbp @ + 1 lit + sbe @ u> 0= and if
		sbp @ 1 lit + sbt @ 2 lit pick sbcp  0 lit over sbt @ + c!
		dup 1 lit + sbp @ + sbp !  -1 lit
	else drop 0 lit 0 lit then
else 0 lit 0 lit then ;
\ sbis ( buf len a n -- flag )  the name read is a (n bytes).
: sbis  rot over = if sbsame else 2drop drop 0 lit then ;
: sbpq
over + sbe !  sbp !
sbnm @ sbget swap sbnl !  sblb @ sbget swap sbll !  and  sbp @ sbe @ = and ;
: sbpa
over + sbe !  sbp !
sbtn @ sbget swap sbtn @ swap sbnm @ sbnl @ sbis and
sbtl @ sbget swap sbtl @ swap sblb @ sbll @ sbis and
0= if 0 lit else
sbp @ sbe @ = if 1 lit else
sbe @ sbp @ - 4 lit u< if 0 lit else
	sbp @ sble@ sbcn !  sbp @ 4 lit + sbca !
	sbca @ sbcn @ + sbe @ u> if 0 lit else
	sbca @ sbcn @ + sbe @ = if 2 lit else 3 lit then then
then then then ;
: sbbun
over + sbe !  sbp !
sbe @ sbp @ - 4 lit u< if 0 lit else
	sbp @ sble@ sbcn !  sbp @ 4 lit + dup sbca !  sbp !
	sbca @ sbcn @ + sbe @ = if
		sbnm @ sbget swap sbnl !  sblb @ sbget swap sbll !  and
	else 0 lit then
then ;
: sbfb variable ;
: sbpt
sbfb @ 0= if 80 lit alloc sbfb ! then
sblb @ sbfb @ sbll @ sbcp  2E lit sbfb @ sbll @ + c!  sbnm @ sbfb @ sbll @ + 1 lit + sbnl @ sbcp
sbfb @ sbll @ sbnl @ + 1 lit + 19 lit sbh @ mghb  sbh @ swap wkcan ;
: sbvf
sbvn !  sbvv !  over + sbe !  sbp !  sbp @ sbca !
sbtn @ sbget swap sbtn @ swap sbnm @ sbnl @ sbis and
sbtl @ sbget swap sbtl @ swap sblb @ sbll @ sbis and
sbe @ sbp @ - 3 lit u< 0= and
0= if 0 lit else
	sbp @ c@ sbtk !  sbp @ 1 lit + c@ sbp @ 2 lit + c@ 8 lit lshift or sbt !  sbp @ 3 lit + sbtv !
	sbtv @ sbt @ + dup sbseq @ 8 lit sbcp  8 lit + dup sbexp @ 8 lit sbcp  8 lit + dup sbpk !  7A0 lit + sbsg !
	sbsg @ CED lit + sbe @ =  sbt @ 101 lit u< and
	\ the value: none empty; an id 32 bytes, each word below the modulus
	sbtk @ 0= if sbt @ 0= and then
	sbtk @ 1 lit = if sbt @ 20 lit = and  8 lit 0 lit do sbtv @ i 2 lit lshift + sble@ 78000001 lit u< and loop then
	\ in force: after now, at most 30 days off
	sbexp @ 4 lit + @ 0=  sbexp @ @ sbvn @ u> and  sbexp @ @ sbvn @ - 278D01 lit u< and  and
	\ the owner's: the key hashes to the value
	dup if sbpk @ sbw @ wkid  sbw @ sbh @ wkcan  sbh @ sbvv @ 20 lit sbsame and then
	dup if drop sbpk @ sbca @ sbsg @ sbca @ - "tab-subname" B lit sbsg @ dilver then
then ;
